A class named Arithmetic with a method named add that takes  integers as parameters and returns an integer denoting their sum.
A class named Adder that inherits from a superclass named Arithmetic.
Your classes should not be be public.


solution:

import java.util.*;

class Arithmetic {
    public int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }
}

class Adder extends Arithmetic {
}

public class Solution {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Adder adder = new Adder();

        System.out.println("My superclass is: " +
            adder.getClass().getSuperclass().getName());

        System.out.println(
            adder.add(20, 22) + " " +
            adder.add(5, 8) + " " +
            adder.add(10, 10)
        );
    }
}
